{"skill":{"slug":"minimax-web-search","displayName":"minimax-web-search"},"version":{"version":"1.0.7","createdAt":1772112435593,"changelog":"- 简化并缩短了 API Key 配置流程说明，移除代理配置自动提取部分。\n- 删除了执行流程的完整示例对话，突出直接操作步骤。\n- 文档说明由“首次需要安装，后续直接调用”优化为“首次需要安装，后续直接步骤4调用”。\n- 其它内容及脚本调用说明未变，功能保持一致。","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"_meta.json","size":137,"sha256":"f7aa08a01623b7440bb9c967dec7991c53da5dcc474fc901f4800c4ff873b789","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3303,"sha256":"39bc46ed39adf257ad91d05f1e1ddca931d709b9133ac43f2ffabf23fb5e9403","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/web_search.py","size":3398,"sha256":"aa648882b6538f19efb0607c3dfe112f5963fe0b8c3c4c595545eebacac08189","contentType":"text/x-python-script"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2249,"sha256":"f28afff6a6c941c27bce736e0b96c5bad1f142a0f3ac7b6f75f0efd760d288ca","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789071144351,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"8e6d1b78c08ab3d581f116432b50c6b94460fd45296d159c3c4b2c96b4ba4b2e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/8e6d1b78c08ab3d581f116432b50c6b94460fd45296d159c3c4b2c96b4ba4b2e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: minimax-web-search\nVersion: 1.0.7\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to two main vulnerabilities. First, the `SKILL.md` instructs the agent to install `uv` using `curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh`, which is a high-risk practice vulnerable to supply chain attacks if the remote script or its source is compromised. Second, the `SKILL.md` also presents a shell injection vulnerability where the user-provided `<搜索查询>` is directly inserted into a shell command (`python3 {curDir}/scripts/web_search.py \"<搜索查询>\"`) without explicit sanitization, potentially allowing an attacker to execute arbitrary commands if the OpenClaw agent does not sanitize input. The `scripts/web_search.py` itself appears to handle the query safely once received as an argument, passing it as a JSON string to the `minimax-coding-plan-mcp` tool, and communicates with the legitimate `https://api.minimaxi.com` endpoint.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779164826863},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":18,"checkedAt":1789071144351},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This web-search skill is purpose-aligned overall, but it asks users or agents to run mutable third-party code and handle API credentials in ways that need review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The runtime launches an external MCP package and passes the MiniMax API key plus the full inherited process environment to it; network access is expected for search, but inheriting all ambient variables is broader than needed.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The setup instructions pipe a remote uv installer directly into sh and install minimax-coding-plan-mcp through uvx without a pinned version or integrity verification, including alternate package indexes.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The activation scope covers generic web-search and current-information requests, while first-run instructions include shell setup, package installation, credential collection, and local config reads/writes without strong consent or scoping boundaries.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill instructs users to save the MiniMax API key in plaintext under ~/.openclaw/config/minimax.json and uses ~/.openclaw/workspace/minimax-output as a persistent output path.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is MiniMax-backed web search, and the script coherently sends a user query through a MiniMax MCP web_search call.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing. Use a safer, pinned installation path for uv and minimax-coding-plan-mcp, avoid curl-pipe-to-shell, store the MiniMax API key in a secret manager or tightly permissioned file, and do not run this skill in an environment containing unrelated sensitive environment variables.","findings":"[TM2] unexpected: The artifact does contain repeated curl ... | sh installer commands. Installing dependencies is setup-related, but direct remote shell execution is broader and riskier than needed for a search skill.\n[SC2] unexpected: The external installer script is fetched and executed without pinning, checksum, signature verification, or inspection; this supports the supply-chain concern.\n[RP1] unexpected: The artifact installs and runs minimax-coding-plan-mcp by package name through uvx without an exact version or lockfile, so reviewed behavior can change after publication.\n[E2] unexpected: The script merges all of os.environ into the MCP subprocess environment. Passing MINIMAX_API_KEY is expected for the integration, but forwarding unrelated ambient secrets is not necessary.\n[TT2] unexpected: The same subprocess environment behavior is present and materially increases the impact of a compromised or unexpected MCP package.\n[AST4] expected: The script uses subprocess.Popen with shell=False and a fixed argument list, so this is not direct shell injection from the query; the remaining concern is execution of an unpinned external package.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending search queries to MiniMax and using an API key are expected, but the artifacts give limited user-facing warning about third-party transmission and plaintext key storage.\n[RA2] expected: Persisting the API key is disclosed in the instructions and supports convenience, but plaintext long-lived storage under the home directory is a real credential exposure concern.\n[LP3] unexpected: The skill uses shell commands, local files, environment variables, networked MCP execution, and persistent config without explicit permission metadata or least-privilege boundaries.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad trigger for ordinary web searches can invoke a workflow that includes setup and credential handling, which is wider than a tightly scoped MiniMax-only search trigger.\n[T03] unexpected: The SARIF remote-payload finding is supported by the SKILL.md installer commands that execute a mutable network script via sh.\n[T08] unexpected: The SARIF dependency finding is supported by both SKILL.md and scripts/web_search.py invoking minimax-coding-plan-mcp without version pinning or artifact verification.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789071144351}}}}}